  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Replace debug assertions with explicit ArgumentOutOfRangeException checks and tighten behavior across Buffer methods for safer runtime behavior.\n      Key changes:\n      - Added validation in Remove, Reserve, Resize, Shift, Unshift, WriteAt and SafeToInt32 to throw clear exceptions for invalid inputs.\n      - Reserve now early-returns if capacity is already sufficient and throws when requested capacity exceeds MaxBufferCapacity; capacity growth logic preserved.\n      - WriteAt overloads for ReadOnlySpan<byte>/char made private and added offset non-negative checks; generic WriteAt validates offsets and dispatches to byte/char paths.\n      - ShiftAt now resizes when offset >= Size (appends) instead of treating as an error; UnshiftAt handles edge cases (offset == Size) and returns/adjusts Size appropriately.\n      - Removed System.Diagnostics using and removed Debug.Assert usages for production-safe checks.\n      - Change DefaultCapacity and MaxRetainedCapacity in Buffer.cs from private const to public static so they can be accessed and modified externally (e.g., for tests or runtime configuration).\n\n      These changes improve robustness by providing predictable exceptions and clearer handling of boundary conditions.",
